# DeskRecordor

DeskRecordor is an early-stage GTK 4 and Libadwaita screen and microphone
recorder for Debian 12 and 13.

> **Development status:** the GTK interface and an FFmpeg-based capture
> prototype are present. X11 capture is experimental; Wayland portal capture
> is not yet a complete end-to-end recording flow. Test carefully before
> relying on recordings.

## Install a Debian package

Download a `.deb` from the [GitHub releases](https://github.com/sheriffhomard/DeskRecordor/releases),
then install it with APT so Debian can resolve its dependencies:

```bash
sudo apt install ./deskrecordor_VERSION_all.deb
```

The package requires GTK 4, Libadwaita, FFmpeg and the desktop portal. A
compatible portal backend and PipeWire/PulseAudio service must also be
available in the desktop session.

To build a package locally, install the Debian build dependencies and run:

```bash
sudo apt install build-essential debhelper dh-python pybuild-plugin-pyproject \
  python3-all python3-setuptools python3-build python3-installer
./build-deb.sh
sudo apt install ./dist/deskrecordor_0.2.0-2_all.deb
```

## Development

Python 3.10 or later is required. To run the current test suite:

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
pytest
```

The package uses a `src/` layout. To run the application during development:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python -m deskrecordor
```

See `docs/` for the project brief and initial architecture notes.
